.TH PSMatrixExpand 3 2025-01-20 "PsyC 0.9.5" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
\fBPSMatrixExpand\fR

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/maths.h>

.I
PSMatrix  
.br
\fBPSMatrixExpand\fR(\fIPSMatrix src\fR, \fIlong add\fR, \fIint keep_src\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a new matrix having the shape of \fIsrc\fR but with the first dimension increased by the value of \fIadd\fR. The original values \fIsrc\fR will be copied to the new matrix, and all the new values belonging to thecexpanded dimension will be initialized to zero.
.br
If \fIkeep_src\fR is zero, the original matrix \fIsrc\fR will be freed.  

.SH RETURN VALUES
The new expanded matrix or:

.RS 4
\[bu] \fIsrc\fR itself if \fIadd\fR is less that one.
.br

\[bu] \fINULL\fR if \fIsrc\fR is \fINULL\fR.
.br

\[bu] \fINULL\fR if memory cannot be allocated.
.br
.RE

.SH SEE ALSO
psyc(1)
